Z||000012||Reality||12-26-2001||08:12 PM||||Well not to rain on the parade, cause I'm probably wrong. But it might be an 88. I have come across several 87's that are titled as 88's. And I own an 85 that is titled as an 86. Just thought I would share before we started accusing people that didn't deserve it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/realitysignature_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||MinnGreenGT||12-26-2001||08:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Reality:<BR><B>Well not to rain on the parade, cause I'm probably wrong. But it might be an 88. I have come across several 87's that are titled as 88's. And I own an 85 that is titled as an 86. Just thought I would share before we started accusing people that didn't deserve it.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, but just because a car is titled incorrectly does not change the way the car was built! It is '87 parts, and '87 VIN (I assume)... and if you tried to get an '88 front suspension piece- you'd be screwed!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Which takes me to the next item- wheel offset.  88 front wheels don't have the offset depth of the earlier ones! (although that may be difficult to determine from a photo). :P<P>This is fun! We need more "mind puzzle" type things like this around here- especially in the winter!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Reality||12-26-2001||10:20 PM||||I was just makeing the point that he might not be lieing. I mean he isn't passing the car off as some "RARE" 88 or that it has the "LOTUS" suspension. He just states that it's an 88. He might not know what he does or does not have. He probably knows that it is a fairly low milesage car and he wants to try and make some money. Just because some of us know what the Fiero is, and is about dosen't mean that everyone else that has one does. Was just trying to make the point that it "might" be an 88. That's all. Have a good one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||soup||12-27-2001||02:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Reality:<BR><B>I was just makeing the point that he might not be lieing. I mean he isn't passing the car off as some "RARE" 88 or that it has the "LOTUS" suspension. He just states that it's an 88. He might not know what he does or does not have. He probably knows that it is a fairly low milesage car and he wants to try and make some money. Just because some of us know what the Fiero is, and is about dosen't mean that everyone else that has one does. Was just trying to make the point that it "might" be an 88. That's all. Have a good one.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would agree but the website says that he bought it brand new.<P>||||reg||1
